module gunbc.roadmap_identity


data roadmap_identity_index_derivation_note: String = "THE INDEX IS DERIVED, NEVER AUTHORED. An earlier cut carried a hand-written list of (identity, slug) rows beside the authority, which created two things that had to be kept in step and could disagree — the DESIGN 3 fork, with a witness standing in for a construction (DESIGN 5). Identity is now a required field on RoadmapNode, so a node without one is unwritable, and everything below is a projection of declared_roadmap_nodes(). There is exactly one place a node's identity can be stated, and the index cannot drift from it because it has no independent existence."

data roadmap_identity_lifecycle_note: String = "PERMANENT NON-REUSE NEEDS A TOMBSTONE, and a base-versus-head diff alone cannot supply it. Without persisted retirement the sequence is: PR A removes node X and its row; a diff gate observes the removal once; after merge X is simply absent from the base registry; PR B mints a new node and reuses X's identity; the next base-versus-head comparison sees an identity that is present in head and absent in base — indistinguishable from a legitimately NEW identity. The reuse passes every check.\\n\\nSo retirement is a state, not a deletion. A Tombstoned row keeps the identity in the registry forever, carries the slug it last wore so historical links still resolve, and names the identity that superseded it when there is one. Retirement is then observable rather than inferred from absence, and 'may never become active again' becomes checkable."

type RoadmapIdentityRecord
  = ActiveIdentity {
      identity: gunbc.roadmap_model.RoadmapNodeIdentity,
      slug: gunbc.roadmap_model.RoadmapNodeId,
    }
  | TombstonedIdentity {
      identity: gunbc.roadmap_model.RoadmapNodeIdentity,
      former_slug: gunbc.roadmap_model.RoadmapNodeId,
      superseded_by: gunbc.roadmap_model.RoadmapNodeIdentity?,
    }

data roadmap_tombstone_roster_note: String = "The first retirement landed 2026-07-31, in the same change that removed its node from declared_roadmap_nodes() — exactly the discipline this roster exists for (a retirement is a state, never a deletion; the failure mode is the 2026-07-27 authority refresh, when a node carrying the only execution contract was removed and nothing noticed). v2-phase-carriers was split by the post-merge verdict on gunbc#7489 into five staged nodes (self-grounding frontier, Translate refusal, inferred-tree completeness, per-kind derivation coverage, target realization gate); its identity is tombstoned with superseded_by naming the split's entry node, so historical links resolve and the identity can never be reused. The 2026-08-01 spine reconciliation (operator verdict on the guarantee lane) retired four more the same way, each superseded_by the recut's entry node: the three monolithic walls whose landed fragments merged at a different grain than the nodes described (floor-method-existence-wall -> method-established-surface-wall via gunbc#7484; floor-call-shape-wall -> call-label-and-surplus-wall via gunbc#7519; floor-inhabitance-wall -> declared-conformance-ground-fragment via gunbc#7484's counted advisory), and the monolithic acceptance door, split into mechanism-then-activation so the door's audit form lands with the carrier instead of after every wall (compiler-accepted-obligation-closure -> accepted-obligation-door-mechanism)."

